3. Hot Reload vs. Hot Restart: 
• Hot Reload (r): Injects updated source code into the running Dart VM and rebuilds the widget tree. Used for UI tweaks and layout adjustments. Preserves application state (takes under 1 second). • Hot Restart (R): Restarts the entire application, resetting the app state completely. Used when modifying main initialization logic, global state, or adding new static assets. 
