3. Security Explanation: 
Connecting applications with the root account breaks the principle of least privilege. If the web application is compromised via SQL injection or a code leak, the attacker gains full control over all databases on the server. 
mysql> CREATE USER 'appuser'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'StrongPassword123!'; mysql> GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON school.* TO 'appuser'@'localhost'; mysql> FLUSH PRIVILEGES; 
Solution Task 3: Python Environment Setup 
1, 2, & 3. Terminal Execution: 
# Create folder & enter 
$ mkdir python_setup_lab && cd python_setup_lab 
# Create virtual environment 
$ python3 -m venv venv 
# Activate virtual environment (macOS/Linux) 
$ source venv/bin/activate 
# (For Windows CMD: venv\Scripts\activate | PowerShell: venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1) 
# Install package & verify 
(venv) $ pip3 install requests 
(venv) $ pip3 list 
# Export to requirements file 
(venv) $ pip3 freeze > requirements.txt 
